  "what_this_measures": "For each held-out block, whether the VISIBLE grid plus the action and click data DETERMINE the next grid. A key is (grid.tobytes(), action, repr(data)); a CONFLICTING key is one observed with two or more different next_grids. Every row beyond the modal outcome of a conflicting key is unpredictable by ANY deterministic engine(grid, action, data), which is the signature this induction task asks the model to write.",
  "headline": "8 of 11 hidden-state games have conflicting keys in the fresh block; 0 of 9 plain-branch games do. The projects hardcoded HIDDEN_STATE_GAME_IDS tuple is therefore independently corroborated from data rather than assumed, and the per-game achievable ceiling on change_accuracy is 1.0 on every plain-branch game and 0.906-0.993 on the hidden-state games that conflict.",
  "consequence_for_this_run": "The PRIMARY is scoped to the plain branch, where the ceiling is a clean 1.0, so no plain-branch zero can be blamed on an unreachable maximum. Hidden-state games are reported against their OWN per-game ceiling, never against 1.0."
}